>> servings: 4
>> source: https://www.nemlig.com/opskrifter/aeggewraps-med-kylling-og-hummusdressing-98003009
>> course: Dinner, Main
>> cuisine: Mexican
>> method: Pan

Shred the @pointed cabbage{0.5} as finely as you can and set it aside for serving.

Rinse and halve the @cucumber{1} lengthways. Scoop out the seeds with a teaspoon, cut into half moons and set aside for serving.

Rinse and quarter the @cherry tomatoes{200%g} and keep them for serving.

Heat a #frying pan{} with the @olive oil{1%tbsp} and fry the @minced chicken{400%g} for ~brown{7%minutes} until cooked through and browned.

Add the @fajita seasoning{5%tsp}, the @water{2%tbsp}, the @salt{1%pinch} and the @pepper{1%pinch} and let the meat simmer over low heat until serving.

Stir the @hummus{150%g} with the juice of the @lemon{1} and the @water{2%tbsp}, then season to taste with salt and pepper.

In a bowl, whisk the @eggs{8} with the @milk{1%dl}, the @salt{1%pinch} and the @pepper{1%pinch} until smooth.

Heat a frying pan to medium-high heat and add the remaining @olive oil{1%tbsp}.

Make the egg wraps one at a time.

Pour some of the egg mixture into the pan and let it set for ~set{3%minutes}, then flip it gently and let it cook for another ~finish{2%minutes}. Slide the wrap onto a plate.

Repeat with the rest of the egg mixture.

Serve the egg wraps topped with the spiced chicken, the crisp cabbage, the cucumber and tomato salad and the hummus dressing.
